  "implementation": [
    "Private class-restricted QAccessibleWidget factory exposes CheckBox role while preserving QLabel rendering and callers.",
    "Qt owns and caches the interface; the widget retains its Python wrapper. No manual interface registration or deletion is performed.",
    "State reads the existing toggle value and inherits current focus/visibility/enabled state. Standard Toggle and inherited widget actions are available only while enabled.",
    "Accessible Toggle and mouse activation use the existing setChecked path, which sends a checked-state-change notification exactly on real changes before the existing toggled signal.",
    "Explicit caller names take precedence; otherwise the full current translated label is exposed even if its painted text is elided."
  ],
